365 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 241 0 R
/E (When you choose to step into a Model United Nations chamber, you are making a conscious decision to engage with the world beyond your own immediate experience. The issues we gather to discuss are not abstract academic puzzles; they are real, pressing global challenges that affect millions of lives every single day. Navigating these problems requires a rare combination of qualities: the courage to stand up for principled positions, the intellectual rigour to analyze complex legal and political frameworks, and the humility to search for pragmatic compromise when opinions diverge. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
366 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 241 0 R
/E (Model United Nations is, at its core, a laboratory for leadership. It is a unique space designed to test your critical thinking, polish your public speaking, and sharpen your ability to negotiate under pressure. Over the course of our sessions, you will be asked to step into shoes that may feel unfamiliar, defend perspectives you might not personally hold, and collaborate with peers who bring vastly different viewpoints to the table. These moments of friction and negotiation are where true diplomacy happens. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
