/P 250 0 R
/E (back to the creation of the Schengen Area in 1985 \(enacted in 1995\), which abolished internal border controls between participating European states. To balance free internal movement with regional security, EU Member States recognized the need for a unified external border policy and a standardized asylum evaluation system. This led to the establishment of the Dublin Convention in 1990, which was later codified into the Dublin II and Dublin III )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 250 0 R
/E (the term to cover individuals who move across international borders primarily for economic, educational, or personal reasons rather than an immediate fear of persecution or violence, meaning they generally operate under the national immigration laws of the host state. Finally, irregular migration refers specifically to the movement of individuals crossing borders outside the established legal, regulatory, or administrative frameworks of destination or transit countries. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
