/P 251 0 R
/T (To manage the crisis, the European Union pursued external diplomatic and financial partnerships with non-EU transit countries. The 2016 EU-Turkey Statement represented an agreement where Turkey committed to securing its borders and accepting the return of irregular migrants arriving in Greece, in exchange for European financial aid and refugee resettlement commitments. Additionally, EU cooperation with Libyan authorities focused on financial and technical support to intercept migrant vessels in the Central Mediterranean. While these external agreements led to reductions in sea arrivals, they drew criticism from international human rights bodies regarding safety concerns, detention conditions, and compliance with international law. )
/E (To manage the crisis, the European Union pursued external diplomatic and financial partnerships with non-EU transit countries. The 2016 EU-Turkey Statement represented an agreement where Turkey committed to securing its borders and accepting the return of irregular migrants arriving in Greece, in exchange for European financial aid and refugee resettlement commitments. Additionally, EU cooperation with Libyan authorities focused on financial and technical support to intercept migrant vessels in the Central Mediterranean. While these external agreements led to reductions in sea arrivals, they drew criticism from international human rights bodies regarding safety concerns, detention conditions, and compliance with international law. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
