/E (A second major issue involves the legality, effectiveness, and humanitarian implications of accelerated border screening and fast-track processing procedures. Under recent reforms, mandatory health, security, and biometric checks are conducted at external borders within an accelerated timeframe. Applicants originating from countries with low statistical asylum approval rates are placed into fast-track border procedures. While proponents contend these measures prevent administrative backlogs and streamline returns, civil society groups and legal scholars argue that accelerated evaluations undermine due process, restrict access to qualified legal counsel, and lead to systematic border detention. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
