/E (an effective means to prevent dangerous sea crossings and dismantle human smuggling operations. However, international human rights organizations and UN rapporteurs argue that outsourcing border control to third-party nations with weaker human rights protections risks bypassing the principle of non-refoulement and violating international law. Furthermore, the continued reintroduction of temporary internal border controls by individual Member States raises questions regarding compliance with Schengen governance and threatens the principle of free internal movement within the Union. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
