/P 253 0 R
/E (Political objectives within the European Parliament mirror these regional and ideological divides. Frontline states prioritize mandatory burden-sharing, operational assistance from Frontex, and direct EU funding for processing infrastructure. Interior states prioritize restricting secondary movements and ensuring strict enforcement of external screening protocols. Within the European Parliament, progressive political groups emphasize expanding legal pathways, funding search-and-rescue operations, and protecting human rights. In contrast, conservative and right-leaning political families focus on border security, expanding the mandate of Frontex, swift deportation of rejected applicants, and expanding externalthird-country agreements. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
