/T (While the agreement drastically reduced sea arrivals in the short term, it ultimately faltered as a long-term solution due to heavy reliance on a single non-EU partner, mounting legal challenges, and deteriorating diplomatic relations. Furthermore, processing backlogs on Greek islands led to severe overcrowding in containment camps, while international oversight bodies criticized the arrangement over human rights standards and non-refoulement risks. Future bilateral partnerships must integrate strict, independent human rights monitoring frameworks and diversify regional diplomatic cooperation rather than over-relying on single transit nations. )
/E (While the agreement drastically reduced sea arrivals in the short term, it ultimately faltered as a long-term solution due to heavy reliance on a single non-EU partner, mounting legal challenges, and deteriorating diplomatic relations. Furthermore, processing backlogs on Greek islands led to severe overcrowding in containment camps, while international oversight bodies criticized the arrangement over human rights standards and non-refoulement risks. Future bilateral partnerships must integrate strict, independent human rights monitoring frameworks and diversify regional diplomatic cooperation rather than over-relying on single transit nations. )
